  "notes": "All 74 pictograms imported from the OLD file's 'Icons Flat' frame (IqEKofKVdD06iF3A1Dlzrz, page 4104:21222, frame 4316:4571). Every component flattened cleanly via figma.flatten() into a single 'Glyph' vector (no unflattened/failed items). Fill (and, for reach-remote and subsea-infrastructure, stroke) colour bound to icon/accent (VariableID:8:43). Documentation frame 'Components / Pictograms' (node 33:74) is 1440 wide x 2760 tall, positioned at x=0 y=1392 (160px below Components / Icons), containing Header and a Grid (33:79) with 74 Tile/<name> children in build order. Six original layer names were vague or duplicated and were renamed based on visual inspection: 'Monitoring copy 4' -> seabed-scanner (crane+box with scan beams over seabed), 'Monitoring copy 9' -> subsea-telemetry (crane+box with wifi signals top and bottom), 'IMR 2' -> seabed-repair (crane+box with wrench tools at seabed), 'Monitoring copy' -> sonar-vessel (vessel over sonar ripples), 'Monitoring' -> global-monitoring (split globe/circle shape), 'IMR' -> maintenance-repair (gear with wrench). Per coordinator correction: each Pictogram/<name> COMPONENT was inserted directly as tile.insertChild(0, comp) rather than instanced, so no Pictogram/* component was ever left loose at the page root; verified at completion via figma.currentPage.findAll filtering top-level COMPONENT nodes named 'Pictogram/*' -> empty array, and Grid child count == 74. | 15 Sep: reach-remote rebuilt unflattened (20 vectors, strokes 2.5/2.28 + fills, bound to icon/accent) because flatten dropped the stroked hull. Names from old layer names may not match imagery: offshore-cables shows a lightning bolt, reach-way shows a head with cycle arrows."
